摘要中的主要功能必须被所选片段支持。优先把改变用途含义的条件写进摘要，不能只藏在limitations。遇到“阶段1骨架”“cloud provider待实现”“匿名thread后续实现”等，摘要明确当前仅本地草稿/审批落盘，不说已实现匿名网络或云端发布。Codex/模型登录适配归coding-development；Oopz等语音房的对话连接归communication-integrations。自述兼容或性能用“作者称/README注明”，不冒充本次验证。
格式示例（仅结构，不是来源事实）：evidence:[{"paragraph_id":"p3s1","fact":"该片段支持的中文转述"}]。请从本次真实输入挑选编号。","role":"system"},{"content":"{"metadata":{"description":"Config-driven lifecycle hooks plugin for DeepSeek Harness","id":"gh:1334777465","install_available":true,"language":"TypeScript","name":"dsh-hooks","slug":"PeterBon/dsh-hooks","topics":["dsh-plugin"]},"paragraphs":[{"id":"p1s1","text":"Config-driven lifecycle hooks plugin for DeepSeek Harness"},{"id":"p2s1","text":"# dsh-hooks"},{"id":"p3s1","text":"Config-driven lifecycle hooks plugin for DeepSeek Harness (dsh)."},{"id":"p4s1","text":"Declare `event -> command` hooks directly in your profile's `cordis.patch.yml` — like Codex CLI / Op"},{"id":"p4s2","text":"enCode hooks, but for dsh. No plugin code required."},{"id":"p5s1","text":"中文文档 | Design | Feishu example | Web GUI"},{"id":"p6s1","text":"## Install"},{"id":"p7s1","text":"One package ships everything (hook engine + Web GUI settings page):"},{"id":"p8s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p9s1","text":"Restart `dsh web`. The settings panel gains a \"Hooks\" section (see Web GUI)."},{"id":"p10s1","text":"## Configure"},{"id":"p11s1","text":"Add a config block to your profile's `cordis.patch.yml`:"},{"id":"p12s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p13s1","text":"Every hook field:"},{"id":"p14s1","text":"| Field | Meaning | Default |"},{"id":"p15s1","text":"| `on` | triggering event (see the event table) | required |\n| `when` | filter `turn/end` by end rea"},{"id":"p15s2","text":"son | all reasons |\n| `match` | field → regex or numeric comparison, all must match; fields are cont"},{"id":"p15s3","text":"ext keys (`tool` / `sessionName` / `sessionId` / `error` / `source` / `cwd` / `content` / `reason` /"},{"id":"p15s4","text":" `turn` / `durationMs` / `toolDurationMs`, …), a field absent from the context never matches. Regexe"},{"id":"p15s5","text":"s test the string form; comparisons (`{ gt: 10000 }` or `'>10000'`, ops `gt` / `gte` / `lt` / `lte` "},{"id":"p15s6","text":"/ `eq`, combinable) apply only to numeric fields and never match non-numeric ones | no filter |\n| `r"},{"id":"p15s7","text":"un` | command spawned through the platform shell (exactly one of `run` / `notify`) | one of the two "},{"id":"p15s8","text":"required |\n| `notify` | built-in notification (exactly one of `run` / `notify`): `channel: webhook` "},{"id":"p15s9","text":"(HTTP JSON; omit `url` to use `DSH_HOOKS_WEBHOOK_URL`, `slack: true` for a one-line summary), `chann"},{"id":"p15s10","text":"el: desktop` (platform balloon/toast), or `channel: feishu` (post the card straight from the plugin "},{"id":"p15s11","text":"using the scan-flow credentials — **no external script**; see the Feishu section) | one of the two r"},{"id":"p15s12","text":"equired |\n| `input` | `env` passes only the `DSH_HOOK_*` variables; `stdin` additionally writes the "},{"id":"p15s13","text":"full context JSON to the command's stdin | `env` |\n| `timeoutMs` | per-run timeout (ms); the process"},{"id":"p15s14","text":" tree is terminated on expiry. On the notify webhook channel it bounds **one request** (default 1000"},{"id":"p15s15","text":"0); the desktop channel is a local balloon whose script intentionally lives ~9 s, so it does not app"},{"id":"p15s16","text":"ly there | 10000 |\n| `retries` | retry count for non-zero exit codes (spawn failures and timeouts ne"},{"id":"p15s17","text":"ver retry) | 0 |\n| `retryDelayMs` | base delay between retries (ms), doubles per attempt, **capped a"},{"id":"p15s18","text":"t 30 s** | 500 |\n| `enabled` | `false` disables the hook without deleting it: the declaration stays,"},{"id":"p15s19","text":" dispatch skips it silently (never counts as a failure) | `true` |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p16s1","text":"## Events (v1)"},{"id":"p17s1","text":"| Event | When it fires | Useful context |"},{"id":"p18s1","text":"| `turn/start` | A turn begins (with `turn/start` hooks, dispatch waits for the turn's first direct "},{"id":"p18s2","text":"user message and attaches its text as `DSH_HOOK_CONTENT`; turns without one dispatch content-less at"},{"id":"p18s3","text":" `turn/end`, see below) | session id, turn, initiating message text |\n| `turn/end` | A turn ends (`c"},{"id":"p18s4","text":"ompleted` / `error` / `aborted` / `blocked` / `max-tokens` / `interrupted` / `forked`) | reason, tur"},{"id":"p18s5","text":"n, duration, content, turn token usage, running subagents |\n| `tree/settled` | A watched session's w"},{"id":"p18s6","text":"hole subagent tree settles (no live child still running) after a turn ended with work handed off | t"},{"id":"p18s7","text":"otal subagents, handoff→settle duration |\n| `step/end` | One step of a turn ends (one model call plu"},{"id":"p18s8","text":"s its tool executions) | turn, step |\n| `tool/call` | The model requests one tool invocation | tool "},{"id":"p18s9","text":"name, call id, raw arguments JSON |\n| `tool/result` | A tool call completes | tool name (resolved), "},{"id":"p18s10","text":"result text, failure identity, wall-clock duration (absent when the pairing call was never seen) |\n|"},{"id":"p18s11","text":" `user/message` | A user-role message appears on the surface | source kind (`user` / `plugin` / …), "},{"id":"p18s12","text":"message text |\n| `approval/asked` | A tool call requests user approval | tool name, call id, approva"},{"id":"p18s13","text":"l id, reason |\n| `approval/decided` | A pending approval gets its outcome (paired with `approval/ask"},{"id":"p18s14","text":"ed` by id) | outcome, tool name (resolved), call id, approval id |\n| `session/title` | The session t"},{"id":"p18s15","text":"itle updates (explicit rename / LLM title / fallback) | new title, source kind |\n| `session/created`"},{"id":"p18s16","text":" | A session is published | session id, cwd |\n| `session/disposed` | A session leaves the registry |"},{"id":"p18s17","text":" session id, cwd |\n| `agent/created` | An agent is published | session id |\n| `agent/disposed` | An "},{"id":"p18s18","text":"agent leaves the registry | session id |\n| `agent/error` | The agent loop reports an error | error t"},{"id":"p18s19","text":"ext |\n| `agent/status` | Agent status transition | status |\n| `hook/failed` | A hook fails consecuti"},{"id":"p18s20","text":"vely past `failedAlertThreshold` (default 3; synthetic, emitted from the outcome stream) | failing h"},{"id":"p18s21","text":"ook summary, consecutive failure count |\n[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p19s1","text":"## Command execution"},{"id":"p20s1","text":"[该节后续省略]"},{"id":"p21s1","text":"#### Proxies, security, and verification"},{"id":"p22s1","text":"- The check uses `req.socket.remoteAddress`, ignoring `X-Forwarded-For`, `X-Real-IP`, and `Forwarded"},{"id":"p22s2","text":"`. Behind Docker/NAT/reverse proxies, this may be a gateway or proxy IP instead of the browser machi"},{"id":"p22s3","text":"ne's IP.\n- Allowlisting a proxy IP allows all clients forwarded by that proxy. A local proxy can als"},{"id":"p22s4","text":"o forward external requests as loopback connections. Enforce client restrictions at the proxy. Loopb"},{"id":"p22s5","text":"ack-only refers to the server's (or container's) loopback connections, not exclusively to browsers o"},{"id":"p22s6","text":"n that machine.\n- `*` removes the source IP restriction from sensitive operations including history "},{"id":"p22s7","text":"access, configuration changes, and hook execution. An IP allowlist is not authentication: protect th"},{"id":"p22s8","text":"ese endpoints with a trusted network or external authentication, and do not expose them directly to "},{"id":"p22s9","text":"untrusted networks.\n- This variable affects only `/dsh-hooks/*`; it does not change listen addresses"},{"id":"p22s10","text":", ports, firewall rules, or other plugins' permissions."},{"id":"p23s1","text":"Request `GET /dsh-hooks/status` from both allowed and denied clients using your actual host and port"},{"id":"p23s2","text":". Requests passing this plugin's check receive the normal status JSON; requests rejected by this plu"},{"id":"p23s3","text":"gin receive HTTP 403:"},{"id":"p24s1","text":"[代码示例省略，未执行]"},{"id":"p25s1","text":"If an allowlisted client still receives this error, confirm the variable reached the actual service "},{"id":"p25s2","text":"process, then check whether the server sees the client IP or a proxy/gateway IP. For connection time"},{"id":"p25s3","text":"outs or refused connections, also check listen addresses, port mappings, and network rules."},{"id":"p26s1","text":"## Security"},{"id":"p27s1","text":"Hooks execute arbitrary commands with the dsh process privileges. Only configure commands you trust."},{"id":"p27s2","text":" Secrets belong in environment variables or the dsh credential store — never in `cordis.patch.yml`."}],"truncated":true}","role":"user"}],"model":"MiniMax-M3.1-Flash","reasoning_effort":"low","stream":false}
